2026-09-08  Oddur Sigurdsson  <oddurs@gmail.com>

	Finish the v0.1 milestone: all eleven items.

	* crates/crabbucket/src/markdown.rs: Return Body { html, headings }.
	Give every heading a stable id and a permalink anchor; honour an
	explicit {#id}.  Highlight fenced code with syntect into scope
	classes, loading the syntax set once per process.
	* crates/crabbucket/src/links.rs (Reason): New enum, distinguishing
	a missing route, a missing asset, a missing anchor, and a relative
	link on the error page.  Check fragments against heading ids; check
	a bare #fragment against the page it was written in.
	* crates/crabbucket/src/error.rs: Drop thiserror; write Display by
	hand so the library can offer render(color).  (Snippet): New; the
	offending line with a caret, at a file-absolute line number.
	(Error::Schema): Replaces Frontmatter and Config, which were the
	same failure.
	* crates/crabbucket/src/style.rs: New file.  Style and StyleSheet:
	component styles beside their components, namespaced, composed by
	the theme, deduplicated by namespace and name together.
	* crates/crabbucket/src/site.rs (Options): New; --out and --base.
	Write content/404.md as 404.html, outside the route set.  Write
	sitemap.xml and robots.txt when site.toml has a url.
	* crates/crabbucket/src/theme.rs (Theme::router_js): Return String,
	since the theme's own class names go into it.
	* crates/crabbucket/tests/build.rs: New file; seventeen tests over
	twelve fixture sites, one per gate.
	* crates/crabbucket-ui/src/styles/: New; six component stylesheets.
	* crates/crabbucket-ui/tests/stylesheet.rs: New file; assert that
	markup and stylesheet cannot drift apart.
	* crates/crabbucket-cli/src/scaffold.rs: New file; `crab new'.
	* crates/crabbucket-cli/src/main.rs: Rewritten parser, with --out,
	--base, --router and --force, and ten tests.
	* doc/crab.1: New file.
	* doc/DESIGN: Revise sections 3, 6 and 10 to match what was built.
	* Makefile (mandir, man1dir): New; install the man page.
	* examples/site: A 404 page; documentation for all of the above.

